    "scientific_name": "Euplectella aspergillum",
    "habitat": "continental_slope",
    "order": 74,
    "notes": "Hexactinellid glass sponge: a tall, gently curved, thin-walled tube (usually 10-30 cm, 2-6 cm wide) of fused silica spicules forming a square-mesh lattice with oblique spiral ridges, widening slightly toward the top, closed by a domed sieve plate; anchored in soft sediment by a tuft of long, hair-thin glassy basal fibres. Pale white to cream. A pair of spongicolid shrimps often lives trapped inside. Filter feeder; the sponge itself is not known to be bioluminescent.",
